# SCENARIO: fix_114_loader_single_scan   SEED: 0   CAMERAS: none   BOTCFG: auto
# Fix #114 items 2/4/5 - one ABI marker scan per `/cavebot reload`, chunked; no temp-copy residue.
# Before: the Lua pre-flight scanned ./libbot_engine.so, then reload() copied it and scanned the copy
# again, both through istreambuf_iterator on the game thread (~260 ms each on the 107 MB .so, measured
# in the WSL mirror; chunked: 18 ms). Run b1_48 shows the old path: "ABI pre-flight ok" then "Copied .so
# to temp path" -> two scans. Now the pre-flight stages + verifies the private copy and reload() opens
# THAT one: "[BotEngineLoader] Using the pre-flight copy ... no second scan".
# A failed copy is refused (running engine kept) and leaves no partial .tmp; stale *.tmp copies are
# removed at startup; with no engine running, the pre-flight says "restart required".
# PRECONDITION: a build containing the fix, normal AI. NOT production during a sensitive window: this
# runs a real `/cavebot reload` of the same .so (bots deactivate/reactivate; ~1 s).
# Acceptance: exactly the single-scan path (>= 1 "Using the pre-flight copy", 0 "Copied .so to temp
# path"), the reload completes, no REFUSED/FAILED.
# Offline replay: python tools/bottest/replay.py <this> runs/b1_48 -> FAILS (old path: 0 / 1).
@srv audit kinds cmd
@srv audit on expect="enabled=on"
@srv cmd _global reload
@srv sleep 20
@srv expect src=srv msg~="BotEngineLoader. Using the pre-flight copy .* no second scan" min=1 within=60
@srv expect-none src=srv msg~="BotEngineLoader. .*Copied .so to temp path" within=60
@srv expect src=srv msg~="BotEngineLoader. Hot-reload complete" min=1 within=60
@srv expect-none src=srv msg~="BotEngineLoader. .*(REFUSED|FAILED)" within=60
@srv expect-none src=srv msg~="Lua Script Error" within=60
@srv audit off
